            "basic_idea": "UNREAL (Unlabeled Nodes Retrieval and Labeling) is an iterative oversampling framework for imbalanced node classification. It leverages unlabeled nodes instead of generating synthetic nodes to smooth label distributions. By using geometric ranking and unsupervised clustering in the embedding space, it effectively selects high-quality nodes with pseudo-labels to enhance model performance in heavily imbalanced scenarios. UNREAL introduces techniques to address geometric imbalance and iteratively updates the training set to improve classification accuracy.",
